/*
 * Whether the two cooking skills can fail, written as the presence of a file:
 * custom_mods\reliable_cooking_on under the game folder, beside Rance10.exe.
 * Delete it and both go back to the odds the game shipped with.
 *
 * The two are 調理準備 (Meal Preparation, Id 1131, 75%) and 菓子作り (Sweets
 * Making, Id 1974, 80%). Both are 処理=7 Preprocess with 効果=60 支援配置: no
 * attack, no target, nothing to hit -- they place the [食券保持中] buff and
 * that is all. So the MISS the battle log prints for them is not an accuracy
 * roll at all. It is SceneBattle@CheckSkillPer, which rolls once against the
 * skill's 確率 column and prints s[3279] ＭＩＳＳ（skill activation failed）
 * when it loses, and the AP is spent either way. docs/cooking-skill-chance.md
 * has the whole path.
 *
 * Which is why raising the number here is the whole change: 確率 is what that
 * one roll compares against, checkRandomPercent is RAND(100) <= percent, and
 * 100 cannot lose.
 *
 * The Id is checked first so that a battle only ever stats the switch file when
 * one of those two skills activates -- every other skill in the game reads its
 * 確率 through this same function, and none of them should be paying for a file
 * lookup. Any Id this does not know gets its own number back, so an .ain with
 * this feature in it and no switch file behaves exactly as an unpatched one.
 *
 * The path is spelled with forward slashes because the .jaf lexer does not take
 * a backslash in a string literal at all, and Windows accepts either separator.
 * It is looked for twice for the reason features/enemy-panel/enemy_info_panel.jaf
 * gives: whether SystemService.GetGameFolderPath() ends in a separator is
 * something the game does not agree with itself about, and trying both spellings
 * settles it without running the game. A path that does not resolve reads as
 * "no file", which is the harmless direction.
 *
 * The skill description is not touched and still reads Buff: <75%>, because it
 * lives in archives/Rance10EX_v1_04/11_スキルデータ.x and features patch the
 * .ain only. Rewriting it would put the change in every build, switch file or
 * not, which is the one thing this feature exists to avoid.
 */
int CookingSkillPercent(int per, int skillId)
{
	if (skillId != 1131 && skillId != 1974) {
		return per;
	}
	string folder = SystemService.GetGameFolderPath();
	if (FileOperation.ExistFile(folder + "custom_mods/reliable_cooking_on")
	 || FileOperation.ExistFile(folder + "/custom_mods/reliable_cooking_on")) {
		return 100;
	}
	return per;
}
